From: Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:03:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 53/59] drm/panthor: BO labels and BO_SET_LABEL ioctl, uAPI 1.4

Mesa (Panthor >= 1.4) names its buffer objects with BO_SET_LABEL so
GPU memory can be attributed to an allocation site when debugging. On
1.0 the call is skipped.

Port the mainline label support carried by the 6.1 rkr7.2 backport: a
label string and lock per GEM object, freed with the object; the
ioctl copies at most PANTHOR_BO_LABEL_MAXLEN bytes from userspace
(longer strings fail with E2BIG); kernel BOs get a fixed name at
creation (FW sections, FW suspend buffers, queue FW interfaces, ring
buffers, job stats, sync objects, heap chunks, heap contexts). Bump
the minor to 4. panthor 1.5 port, 8.0p15.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P6itje71iKPFBX7YKkfvRo
